in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @mirror/store

# @mirror/store/git — the git-backed namespaced wire species under
# @mirror/store.
#
# A prism that imports `in @mirror/store/git` declares its content IS
# one realization of the @mirror/store six-op surface at git-backed
# wire altitude — content-addressed objects living under a namespaced
# subdirectory of a host repository's `.git/` (e.g. `.git/mirror/`),
# pollution-free of the working tree, traveling with clones if refs
# are pushed.
#
# === The recognition (path α, closes the substrate-decl drift) ===
#
# This shard discharges Reed's drift observation logged at
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror` commit `60f5b7d` ("Substrate-decl drift
# observation (2026-06-28, Mara)"): the `NamespacedGitStore` Rust
# surface in `fragmentation/vcs/git/src/namespaced.rs` exposes verbs
# (`open` / `insert_persistent` / `get_persistent` / `set_ref` /
# `get_ref` / `flush` / `path`) that did not line up by simple rename
# with @mirror/store's six-op surface (`read` / `write` / `exists` /
# `diff` / `walk` / `verify`).
#
# Alex's 2026-06-30 substrate-pull decision: path (α) — admit the
# wire altitude as a REAL altitude of the substrate. The wire is now
# a declared altitude of the substrate, not implementation detail
# routed around the substrate-decl surface. The six-op surface
# remains canonical at @mirror/store altitude; this species' wire
# verbs carry the actual `NamespacedGitStore` vocabulary and declare
# HOW they DISCHARGE to the inherited surface.
#
# === Family placement: two-tier, no intermediate species-root ===
#
# Mirrors the @reality/algebra/* pattern in spirit (family + species)
# but two-tier not three-tier: @mirror/store is itself functionally
# specific to storage, so no `algebra` qualifier is needed between
# family-root and species. The species sits directly under
# @mirror/store.
#
# The species roster (forward-promised at
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror`'s species-roster paragraph):
#
#   Landed:
#     @mirror/store/git    THIS SHARD — git-backed namespaced wire
#                          (`fragmentation/vcs/git`).
#
#   Forward-promised (consumer-pull):
#     @mirror/store/mem    in-memory wire (testing + ephemeral).
#     @mirror/store/s3     object-store wire (cloud).
#     @mirror/store/oci    OCI artifact wire (registry-backed).
#     @mirror/store/<...>  other species when consumers pull.
#
# === The wire surface (`NamespacedGitStore` vocabulary) ===
#
# Canonical Rust impl: `fragmentation/vcs/git/src/namespaced.rs`
# (module path `namespaced`; NOT re-exported at crate root per the
# `bootstrap/tests/fragmentation_git_bridge.rs` discovery loop —
# importers use `fragmentation_git::namespaced::NamespacedGitStore`).
#
# The species' wire actions name the methods that surface on the
# Rust impl. Each is a typed lambda whose obligation block (`\`) is
# discharged at the realisation boundary by binding to the
# corresponding `NamespacedGitStore` method.
#
# - `open(path, namespace)`        the constructor; discovers the
#                                  `.git/` from `path` (walking up;
#                                  worktree-aware), creates
#                                  `.git/<namespace>/` with the
#                                  frgmnt store structure (objects/,
#                                  refs/). The default cache size is
#                                  16 MiB at the Rust altitude (the
#                                  substrate altitude does not pin
#                                  the number — `open_with_cache` is
#                                  the variant the realisation calls
#                                  when a non-default budget is
#                                  required).
# - `insert_persistent(store, key, fractal, size)`
#                                  insert a content-addressed
#                                  fragment with disk persistence
#                                  (eviction writes to disk). `key`
#                                  is the content-address (oid)
#                                  string; `fractal` is the
#                                  fragmentation-altitude
#                                  `Fractal<String>` carrier; `size`
#                                  is the byte-size for cache
#                                  accounting.
# - `get_persistent(store, key)`   fetch a fragment with disk
#                                  fallback (cache miss reads from
#                                  `.git/<namespace>/objects/`).
#                                  Returns `imperfect` carrying the
#                                  fragment on success and opacity
#                                  on absence/drift.
# - `set_ref(store, ref_name, oid)`
#                                  write a named ref pointing at an
#                                  oid (e.g. `set_ref("HEAD",
#                                  root_oid)`). Refs live under
#                                  `.git/<namespace>/refs/`.
# - `get_ref(store, ref_name)`     read a named ref; returns
#                                  `imperfect` carrying the oid on
#                                  success and opacity on absence.
# - `flush(store)`                 flush all cached entries to disk.
#                                  The cache invariant: after
#                                  `flush`, `cached_len` is zero
#                                  and every inserted-persistent
#                                  fragment is on-disk-resident.
# - `path(store)`                  the store directory path (e.g.
#                                  `.git/mirror/`). The wire's
#                                  self-location carrier.
#
# === The discharge map: wire verbs -> six-op surface ===
#
# The species inherits the canonical six-op surface from
# @mirror/store (`read` / `write` / `exists` / `diff` / `walk` /
# `verify`). The wire verbs above are this species' specialization;
# the species shard declares HOW each canonical op DISCHARGES through
# the wire's vocabulary at the git-backed altitude.
#
# This is the substrate-decl honesty Alex's path-α decision turns on:
# the six-op surface stays canonical at @mirror/store; the wire verbs
# stay canonical at the species altitude; the discharge map names
# the bridge.
#
#   read(oid)              <= get_persistent(store, oid)
#                              The canonical read is the cache-with-
#                              disk-fallback fetch; opacity on miss
#                              is the wire's standard imperfect.
#
#   write(bytes)           <= insert_persistent(store, oid_of(bytes),
#                                               fractal_of(bytes),
#                                               size_of(bytes))
#                          +  set_ref(store, ref_name, oid_of(bytes))
#                              The canonical write is content-
#                              addressed insert at this wire; the
#                              `set_ref` companion is named here
#                              because at the @mirror/store altitude
#                              the ref-update is part of `write`'s
#                              "this content is now reachable"
#                              semantics (e.g. `mirror init`'s root
#                              splinter becomes reachable through
#                              `HEAD`). The realisation MAY split
#                              the two when only one half is needed
#                              (e.g. raw insert without ref change).
#
#   exists(oid)            <= get_persistent(store, oid).is_some
#                              The canonical exists is presence of
#                              the content-address in the cache-
#                              with-disk fallback. `verdict`'s
#                              `partial(confidence)` arm fires when
#                              the oid is cache-resident but the
#                              disk store has not yet been queried
#                              (rare; documented at
#                              @mirror/store.exists).
#
#   diff(a, b)             <= compute_delta(
#                               get_persistent(store, a),
#                               get_persistent(store, b))
#                              The canonical diff is the content-
#                              addressed delta between two fetched
#                              fragments. Opacity is the @mirror
#                              /store.diff `imperfect` shape
#                              (`partial(opacity_map)` when no
#                              common ancestor; `failure(reason)`
#                              when one isn't present).
#                              `compute_delta` is the inherited
#                              substrate operation — not a wire
#                              verb; the wire only fetches the
#                              raw fragments.
#
#   walk(root)             <= walk_closure_via_get_persistent(store,
#                                                              root)
#                              The canonical walk is the OID-graph
#                              closure of children under the root
#                              splinter, reached by repeated
#                              `get_persistent` calls on each
#                              child oid (the closure IS the
#                              lockfile per @mirror/store.walk).
#                              `walk_closure_via_get_persistent` is
#                              an inherited @mirror/store-altitude
#                              traversal operation; the wire's role
#                              is to fetch the fragments the
#                              traversal asks for.
#
#   verify(oid, bytes)     <= hash(bytes) == oid
#                              The canonical verify is byte-equality
#                              between the re-hashed content and
#                              the claimed oid; the wire does not
#                              participate (the @mirror/store-
#                              altitude hash algebra discharges).
#                              Named here for completeness: the
#                              integrity check is INDEPENDENT of
#                              which species is wiring the bytes;
#                              `verify` discharges identically at
#                              every @mirror/store/* species.
#
# The ref operations (`set_ref` / `get_ref`) are species-private
# wire verbs that do NOT bind to the six-op surface — they extend
# it. Refs are the wire's address book on top of the content-address
# foundation. The species exports `set_ref` / `get_ref` as
# additional vocabulary callers may use when the wire is known to
# be this species; consumers that want to stay portable across
# species use only the six-op surface.
#
# `flush` and `path` are species-private control verbs that name
# wire-altitude lifecycle and self-location; they do NOT bind to
# the six-op surface either. They are exported so realisations can
# observe cache invariants and locate the store on disk.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Content-addressed       git's `.git/objects/` is the canonical
#   storage in `.git/`      content-addressed storage in `.git/`;
#                           the namespace pattern lifts the same
#                           discipline to a non-pollution sibling
#                           directory.
#   Namespaced refs         git's `refs/namespaces/<ns>/` discipline
#                           (since 2011, gitnamespaces(7)); the same
#                           per-namespace ref-isolation pattern but
#                           specialized to this species' on-disk
#                           layout (`.git/<namespace>/refs/`).
#   Cache-with-disk-fallback the LRU + on-disk content-addressed
#                           pattern used by `fragmentation`'s
#                           `FrgmntStore` (the wire's underlying
#                           store).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-init.md (the mirror-init loop
#               that pulled on this species' admission);
#               docs/scouts/2026-06-27-taut-fragmentation-git-store-
#               for-mirror-init.md (the Rust-surface scout that
#               first named the drift).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]
#                       (the Rust impl IS the substrate at the wire
#                        altitude; this shard names the species
#                        whose Rust realisation lives there),
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                       (imperfect / verdict / transparency are
#                        substrate vocabulary; the wire actions
#                        return them, not ad-hoc Option/Result),
#                      [[architecture-mirror-store-vs-spectral-db]]
#                       (the @mirror/store OPEN gate this species
#                        realizes at git-backed wire altitude;
#                        @spectral/db remains the CLOSED engine
#                        on top — this species sits below that
#                        boundary),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (wire actions
#                        return typed `imperfect<...>` shapes, not
#                        bare unions; `usize` is a typed scalar via
#                        the cli/lens precedent's `int` lifting),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the wire altitude was implicit in every
#                        prior `NamespacedGitStore` reference; this
#                        shard makes the altitude addressable as a
#                        substrate-decl object — the substrate had
#                        the wire all along; it just was not yet
#                        named).
# Related shards: store.mirror (the family-root this species
#                  inherits the six-op surface from; the species-
#                  roster paragraph names this shard as the first
#                  landed species),
#                 glass.mirror (verdict / imperfect / transparency;
#                  the wire actions return them).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/store/git.mirror` declares `@mirror/store/git` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

prism @mirror/store/git <= @mirror/store {
  # Git-backed namespaced wire species under @mirror/store. The 5-op
  # gauge action at this species' altitude operates over
  # `git_store` — the typed handle for one open NamespacedGitStore.
  # Per-altitude wire verbs below specialize the inherited six-op
  # surface (read / write / exists / diff / walk / verify) by
  # discharging them through `NamespacedGitStore` method calls.
  focus git_store
  project git_store
  split git_store
  shift git_store
  settle git_store
}

# === The git_store handle ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one open
# `NamespacedGitStore` instance. The realisation layer
# (`fragmentation/vcs/git/src/namespaced.rs::NamespacedGitStore`)
# implements the carrier; the substrate altitude declares the typed
# handle wire actions take and return.
#
# Construction: via `open` (below); never directly. Equality is
# realisation-instance identity, not content-identity (two `open`
# calls against the same `.git/<namespace>/` return distinct handles
# that observe the same on-disk state).
type git_store = ref

# === The fractal carrier ===
#
# The fragmentation-altitude fragment carrier the wire moves. Per
# `fragmentation/src/fragment.rs::Fractal<String>` (the concrete
# realisation `NamespacedGitStore` parameterizes on). At the
# substrate altitude this is a typed reference; the realisation
# layer binds it to `Fractal<String>`.
#
# The wire actions take and return `fractal` on insert/get because
# the `NamespacedGitStore` API operates at fragment granularity
# (not raw `bytes`). The @mirror/store-altitude `read` / `write`
# canonical ops take `bytes`; the discharge from canonical-`write`
# to wire-`insert_persistent` is responsible for going `bytes` ->
# `fractal` via the fragmentation-altitude encoder
# (`fragmentation::encoding::encode`).
type fractal = ref

# === usize — cache-accounting byte-size scalar ===
#
# The size carrier `insert_persistent` takes for cache accounting.
# Lifted from the substrate scalar floor as a typed reference per
# the cli/lens `type int = ref(scalar/int)` precedent. The wire
# does NOT enforce that the declared size equals the fragment's
# actual on-wire byte count; the realisation layer's cache uses
# the value as an accounting hint.
type usize = ref(scalar/int)

# === ref_name — the wire's named-ref string ===
#
# Refs in `.git/<namespace>/refs/` are addressed by string name
# (e.g. `"HEAD"`, `"boot"`). Declared as a typed reference per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] so call sites do not pass bare
# `scalar/string` where the type system can distinguish ref-names
# from arbitrary strings.
type ref_name = ref(scalar/string)

# === namespace_name — the wire's namespace-segment string ===
#
# The `<namespace>` segment in `.git/<namespace>/` (e.g.
# `"mirror"`, `"spectral"`, `"notes/mirror"`). Same typing
# discipline as `ref_name`: bare strings would let unrelated
# string values flow through `open`. The realisation layer accepts
# slash-separated nested namespaces (per `NamespacedGitStore`'s
# `open_nested_namespace` test).
type namespace_name = ref(scalar/string)

# === The wire actions (`NamespacedGitStore` vocabulary) ===
#
# Each action's `\` obligation block discharges at the realisation
# boundary by binding to the corresponding `NamespacedGitStore`
# method. The signatures mirror the Rust impl's method surface;
# the substrate altitude declares the typed shape callers may rely
# on regardless of which realisation binds.

# open(path, namespace) — discover `.git/` from `path` (walking
# up; worktree-aware), create `.git/<namespace>/` with the frgmnt
# store structure, return the typed handle. Failure modes:
# `path` is not inside a git repository (returns
# `failure(not_a_git_repo)` via the wire's imperfect lifting);
# I/O failure on directory creation.
open(path: ~d, namespace: namespace_name) -> imperfect<git_store, ref, transparency(ref)> { \ }

# insert_persistent(store, key, fragment, size) — insert a
# content-addressed fragment with disk persistence. Idempotent
# on `key` (re-inserting the same key with byte-equal content is
# a cache-update no-op; the on-disk file is content-addressed).
# The verdict surface is the wire's success/partial/failure
# triplet: `pass` on insert; `partial` on cache-pressure
# eviction-to-disk that succeeded; `failure(reason)` on I/O.
insert_persistent(store: git_store, key: oid, fragment: fractal, size: usize) -> verdict { \ }

# get_persistent(store, key) — fetch a fragment with disk
# fallback. The wire's standard imperfect: success carries the
# fragment; partial carries a stale-cache hint; failure(reason)
# carries oid-not-present.
get_persistent(store: git_store, key: oid) -> imperfect<fractal, ref, transparency(ref)> { \ }

# set_ref(store, name, oid) — write a named ref pointing at an
# oid. Verdict on the write: `pass` on success; `failure(reason)`
# on I/O. The realisation layer guarantees atomicity within one
# `set_ref` call (no torn writes).
set_ref(store: git_store, name: ref_name, target: oid) -> verdict { \ }

# get_ref(store, name) — read a named ref. The wire's standard
# imperfect: success carries the target oid; failure(reason)
# carries ref-not-present.
get_ref(store: git_store, name: ref_name) -> imperfect<oid, ref, transparency(ref)> { \ }

# flush(store) — flush all cached entries to disk. After `flush`,
# every inserted-persistent fragment is on-disk-resident and the
# cache is empty (the realisation invariant per
# `NamespacedGitStore::flush`'s `cached_len() == 0` post-condition).
# `verdict`'s `partial(confidence)` arm fires when some entries
# flushed and others failed (rare; surfaces I/O failure shape).
flush(store: git_store) -> verdict { \ }

# path(store) — the store directory path (e.g. `.git/mirror/`).
# The wire's self-location carrier; called by realisations that
# need to address the on-disk store from outside the typed handle
# (e.g. for diagnostic output; for sibling tools that walk the
# directory directly).
path(store: git_store) -> ~d { \ }

out @mirror/store/git
out git_store
out fractal
out usize
out ref_name
out namespace_name
out open
out insert_persistent
out get_persistent
out set_ref
out get_ref
out flush
out path
